E["quest:92415"] = {t="quest",n="Remember That I Love You",z="ruinsoflordaeron",s="In the Ruins of Lordaeron, a stained letter calls for a missing child. Torn from parchment among the graves, it speaks of a child from the Heartweaver family. You carry it south to the orphanage in Stormwind City, hoping to learn what became of them.",h="In the Ruins of Lordaeron, a stained letter calls for a missing child.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Ruins",b="The ruined graveyard bears the marks of the Third War. Among grounds haunted by the undead, someone found a torn, blood-stained letter. It speaks of a missing child from the Heartweaver family. Prince Arthas and the Scourge swept through the kingdom and shattered their lives.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Orphanage",b="Lordaeron fell, and the Undercity now fills the catacombs below. Refugees who escaped south scattered across the Alliance kingdoms. In Stormwind City, Orphan Matron Nightingale cares for children left without parents by the wars. You bring her the blood-stained letter, hoping she can identify a surviving Heartweaver child and give the family some closure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the blood-stained letter found?",a="The torn, stained parchment was found in a graveyard in the Ruins of Lordaeron, where restless dead and Forsaken forces roam.",al={"where to find letter","parchment location","where does this quest start"}},{q="Who is the Heartweaver family?",a="Little is known about the Heartweaver family. Their letter speaks of a missing child and raises hope that the child escaped south to an Alliance shelter.",al={"heartweaver","who are the heartweavers","heartweaver lore"}},{q="Who is Orphan Matron Nightingale?",a="Orphan Matron Nightingale oversees the Stormwind Orphanage in Cathedral Square. She gives food, shelter, and guidance to children orphaned by the recent wars.",al={"nightingale","matron nightingale","orphan matron"}},{q="Why take a Lordaeron keepsake all the way to Stormwind?",a="When the Scourge overran Lordaeron, many orphaned children were evacuated south to the Kingdom of Stormwind. The parchment points you to the orphan matron in Stormwind City, who may know more.",al={"why stormwind","why send it to nightingale"}},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="The journey leads to Orphan Matron Nightingale in Stormwind City's Cathedral Square, placing it in Alliance hands.",al={"horde version","can horde do this"}},{q="What state are the Ruins of Lordaeron in right now?",a="The surface ruins of Capital City are mostly deserted and crumbling, with lingering undead. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken have fortified their underground capital, the Undercity, in the crypts below.",al={"ruins of lordaeron status","who controls lordaeron ruins"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Lordaeron lineage, this parchment recalls families torn apart when Capital City fell to Prince Arthas and the Scourge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you carry the letter safely to Stormwind, honoring the northern families torn apart when Lordaeron fell."},kw={"blood-stained letter","capital city","heartweaver","orphan matron nightingale","remember that i love you","ruins of lordaeron","stormwind orphanage"},rel={"npc:orphan-matron-nightingale","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="22",id=92415},src={"In-game quest text: Remember That I Love You"},fv=true}
E["quest:95189"] = {t="quest",n="Crest of Lordaeron",z="ruinsoflordaeron",s="In the ruins of Capital City, a weathered Crest of Lordaeron survives from the fallen northern kingdom. Relics like it are scarce, and Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City is eager to claim one.",h="In the ruins of Capital City, a weathered Crest of Lordaeron survives from the fallen northern kingdom.",sec={{t="A Shattered Heritage",b="The Scourge left Lordaeron's palaces and archives in ruins beneath the shadow of the Undercity. Its proud insignias were destroyed or left to decay, so few relics bearing the royal crest remain. A weathered crest from the northern ruins keeps a piece of human history.",sp=0},{t="Refuge in the South",b="After the Third War, thousands of refugees fled south from Lordaeron toward the Kingdom of Stormwind. They carried memories of home. In Stormwind City, Lady Dena Kennedy seeks remnants of their homeland. For those who left the north behind, a crest like this is a cherished link to Lordaeron.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crest of Lordaeron?",a="The Crest of Lordaeron is a weathered emblem bearing the kingdom's official mark. It survived the Scourge's fall of Lordaeron and remains a historical relic for human survivors.",al={"crest of lordaeron","what is crest of lordaeron","lordaeron crest item"}},{q="Who wants the Crest of Lordaeron?",a="Lady Dena Kennedy in Stormwind City wants the crest. She collects and preserves rare artifacts from Lordaeron.",al={"who takes the crest","where do i bring crest of lordaeron","crest turn in"}},{q="Where was the crest found?",a="The crest was recovered from the Ruins of Lordaeron in Tirisfal Glades. The ruined capital lies above the Undercity, the Forsaken stronghold.",al={"crest location","ruins crest","where to get crest"}},{q="Why are artifacts from Lordaeron so rare?",a="Few Lordaeron artifacts survived the kingdom's swift fall during the Third War. The Scourge slaughtered its people and ruined its estates, while the Forsaken rose in the north.",al={"why are lordaeron relics rare","lordaeron artifacts rarity"}},{q="Why does Stormwind care about relics of Lordaeron?",a="Stormwind welcomed refugees, knights, and nobles fleeing Lordaeron's devastation. Preserving its relics honors the fallen northern kingdom and keeps its human heritage alive.",al={"why stormwind cares","stormwind lordaeron relics"}},{q="Who is Lady Dena Kennedy?",a="Lady Dena Kennedy is a noblewoman in Stormwind City who seeks to salvage heirlooms and other historical remnants of Lordaeron.",al={"lady dena kennedy","who is dena kennedy"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, especially if your family came from the north, the crest recalls the great kingdom that once led the Alliance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Lordaeron's emblem as a mark of the Alliance's founding. Recovering it keeps the Scourge and Forsaken from erasing that symbol."},kw={"crest of lordaeron","heraldry","lady dena kennedy","lordaeron","relic","ruins of lordaeron","stormwind","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:stormwind","topic:lordaeron","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="22",id=95189},src={"In-game quest text: Crest of Lordaeron"},fv=true}
E["quest:95195"] = {t="quest",n="Bloodied Insignia",z="ruinsoflordaeron",s="In Lordaeron's blighted ruins, Bloodied Insignias bear the old Alliance crests of fallen defenders. Many soldiers' families fled south to Stormwind during the Third War.",h="In Lordaeron's blighted ruins, Bloodied Insignias bear the old Alliance crests of fallen defenders.",sec={{t="Tokens of the Fallen",b="Prince Arthas returned with the Scourge and laid waste to Lordaeron. Its great army was overwhelmed, and countless soldiers died defending the capital and the lands around it. Rusted armor and bloodstained brass are all that remain of many who fought.\n\nThe old Alliance insignias belonged to those who stood against the undead. Trampled into soil and rubble, the medals recall Lordaeron's last defense.",sp=0},{t="A Messenger for the Exiles",b="Many survivors fled south across the sea and settled in Stormwind City. Alliance and kinship bind the two human realms, and families in the south still seek news of loved ones lost in the north.\n\nGeneral Marcus Jonathan commands Stormwind's city guard and takes custody of the bloodied insignias. He preserves the defenders' memory and helps their surviving families learn their fate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Bloodied Insignias?",a="They are military medals worn by Lordaeron soldiers who fought and died under the Alliance banner during the Third War.",al={"bloodied insignia item","what is this insignia","insignia lore"}},{q="Where are these insignias found?",a="They are found throughout the Ruins of Lordaeron in Tirisfal Glades, where the kingdom's defenders made their last stand against the Scourge.",al={"where do insignias drop","insignia location","ruins of lordaeron badges"}},{q="Why does General Marcus Jonathan want them?",a="General Marcus Jonathan commands Stormwind City's guard, where many northern refugees now live. He gathers the medals to honor Lordaeron's fallen and help their living relatives find closure.",al={"who is marcus jonathan","why give them to stormwind","marcus jonathan insignia"}},{q="Why were Lordaeron soldiers wearing Alliance insignias?",a="The original Alliance was forged in Lordaeron under King Terenas Menethil II to defeat the Old Horde. Lordaeron led the Alliance of Lordaeron through the Second and Third Wars.",al={"lordaeron alliance crest","alliance of lordaeron badge"}},{q="What happened to the soldiers who wore these medals?",a="They were killed during the Third War, when Prince Arthas Menethil betrayed the realm, killed his father, and unleashed the Scourge on the capital.",al={"what killed the soldiers","fate of lordaeron soldiers"}},{q="Are there still living relatives of these soldiers?",a="Yes. Thousands of citizens and soldiers fled Lordaeron during the plague and Scourge invasions, and found sanctuary in the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"lordaeron refugees stormwind","who misses these soldiers"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, these badges recall the fall of the greatest human kingdom and connect Stormwind's refugees with their fallen kin in the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, returning these medals to General Marcus Jonathan honors the soldiers who died defending their people.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you honor the lost brothers and sisters of the Knights of the Silver Hand by retrieving medals from those who fought beside the order in the capital."},kw={"alliance","bloodied insignia","lordaeron","marcus jonathan","refugees","ruins of lordaeron","stormwind","third war"},rel={"npc:general-marcus-jonathan","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:lordaeron","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={level="22",id=95195},src={"In-game quest text: Bloodied Insignia"},fv=true}
E["zone:ruinsoflordaeron"] = {t="dungeon",n="Ruins of Lordaeron",z="ruinsoflordaeron",s="Above Undercity, the Ruins of Lordaeron still shelter horrors from the fallen capital. Prince Arthas and the Scourge brought the human kingdom to ruin during the Third War. Now the Alliance and Horde venture across the surface to reclaim relics of the past or purge its threats.",h="Above Undercity, the Ruins of Lordaeron still shelter horrors from the fallen capital.",sec={{t="A Fallen Empire's Courtyard",b="Capital City once held the crown of the Eastern Kingdoms. King Terenas Menethil II sat on its throne, and human civilization stood at its heart. When Prince Arthas returned from Northrend, he killed his father in the throne room and unleashed the undead upon the people.\n\nThe Forsaken now dwell in the catacombs below, in Undercity. Above them, the surface remains a forsaken twilight zone. Broken arches and weed-choked cobbles shelter feral beasts such as Witherfang and deranged remnants of the past.",sp=0},{t="Torment and Pestilence",b="Restless dead are not the only danger in the ruined grounds. Apothecaries and sinister figures such as viktor the vile test new plagues in the shadows, while twisted experiments such as the abandoned roam freely.\n\nWrathful spirits such as rath'mael and cursed retainers such as The Baron haunt the collapsed halls, trapped in endless torment. They strike at any living or undead trespasser who crosses their path.",sp=0},{t="Ghosts of the Royal Guard",b="Spectral defenders linger among the upper ruins, with a ghostly Lordaeron Captain among them. Still bound to their shattered oaths, these apparitions see anyone nearing the throne as an invader. Putting the Captain and their soldiers to rest ends a bitter vigil that has endured since the capital fell.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Ruins of Lordaeron dungeon located?",a="The Ruins of Lordaeron dungeon occupies the surface of Capital City in Tirisfal Glades, directly above the entrance network leading down to the Forsaken capital of Undercity.",al={"ruins of lordaeron location","where is lordaeron dungeon","undercity dungeon entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are both the Horde and Alliance interested in this place?",a="The Alliance ventures into Lordaeron to recover lost family heirlooms, gather royal crests, and bring peace to fallen ancestors. The Horde, especially the Forsaken, seeks to secure Undercity's perimeter and obtain research samples for the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague.",al={"why go to lordaeron ruins","alliance quests lordaeron","horde quests lordaeron"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Viktor the Vile?",a="viktor the vile is a sinister figure exploiting the ruins' lawlessness with foul experiments. His work adds to the corruption and twisted abominations infesting the upper capital.",al={"viktor the vile lore","who is viktor the vile"},it="identity"},{q="What is 'The Abandoned' encountered in the ruins?",a="the abandoned is a grotesque undead monstrosity left behind in the ruins. Like many patchwork horrors created during or after the Scourge's conquest, it wanders the derelict chambers aimlessly and attacks anything it encounters.",al={"the abandoned boss","who is the abandoned"},it="threat"},{q="What does defeating the Lordaeron Captain mean for the story?",a="Defeating the spectral Lordaeron Captain frees a high-ranking royal defender from a perpetual, maddening duty. Bound by honor since the Scourge's first massacre, the Captain has guarded a destroyed kingdom for years, and that vigil has endured since the capital fell. Laying the Captain to rest ends an agonizing cycle of phantom servitude and lets the bloodied insignia be reclaimed.",al={"defeating lordaeron captain","lordaeron captain significance","what happens when captain dies"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Is the Ruins of Lordaeron separate from the Undercity?",a="Yes. The Forsaken make their home in Undercity's caverns below, while the surface ruins remain an active combat zone filled with restless ghosts, feral predators, and experimental threats the Forsaken have not fully eradicated.",al={"is undercity in this dungeon","ruins vs undercity"},it="place"},{q="What is this place, the Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="You stand in the shattered remains of Capital City, once the jewel of human civilization and the heart of the Kingdom of Lordaeron. During the Third War, Prince Arthas betrayed his kingdom, slaughtered his father King Terenas in the throne room above, and unleashed the undead Scourge upon its streets. Today, its broken arches and scorched towers sit above the subterranean Undercity, serving as a bitter memorial to the kingdom that fell.",al={"what is lordaeron ruins","ruins of lordaeron lore","what was this place"},it="place",add="1b77984b",nx={8,9}},{q="Who lived here before it was ruined?",a="This city was the home of humanity's greatest northern kingdom, governed by the Menethil dynasty. Nobles, priests of the Holy Light, soldiers, and hundreds of thousands of common folk once walked these paved streets. Tragically, many of those former citizens never truly left; struck down by the plague, their reanimated corpses make up both the mindless Scourge haunting the Plaguelands and the liberated Forsaken now inhabiting the caverns below.",al={"who lived here before","lordaeron original people","who was here first"},it="residents",add="eb89374f"},{q="Why is it all broken and burnt?",a="When Prince Arthas returned with Frostmourne, he slew King Terenas and turned the city over to the Scourge. Undead horrors rampaged through the avenues, burning buildings and butchering anyone who attempted to resist. Later, during the civil war among the undead, Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken battled dreadlords and lingering Scourge legions across these very courtyards, tearing down whatever remained of the city's grand architecture.",al={"why is lordaeron destroyed","how was lordaeron burnt","why is it in ruins"},it="ruin",add="6e6195fd"},{q="Who destroyed Lordaeron?",a="The kingdom was shattered from within by its own crown prince, Arthas Menethil, under the corrupting whisper of the Lich King. Dispatched to stop the Cult of the Damned and their plague of undeath, Arthas grew ruthless, took up the cursed runeblade Frostmourne in the frozen north, and surrendered his soul. Returning home as a death knight, he struck down his father and delivered the city into the claws of the Scourge.",al={"who ruined lordaeron","who brought down lordaeron","destroyer of lordaeron"},it="history",add="dd470a5c",nx={11,12}},{q="Where is Arthas now?",a="Arthas left the ruined continent of Lordaeron years ago, sailing back across the Great Sea to Northrend when the Lich King was threatened by the demon hunter Illidan Stormrage. He fought his way up the icy spire of the Frozen Throne and has vanished from common sight in the frozen wastes, leaving behind a kingdom shattered into rival factions of undead and survivors.",al={"where did arthas go","where is prince arthas","arthas location"},it="target",add="f5a9164f"},{q="Did anyone escape the city?",a="A fortunate few escaped the slaughter. Prior to the final collapse, the sorceress Jaina Proudmoore heeded a mysterious prophet's warnings and led thousands of human refugees across the sea to Kalimdor, where they established the port of Theramore. Others fled south toward the Kingdom of Stormwind, or took up holy arms to fight back, forming the fanatical Scarlet Crusade and the vigilant Argent Dawn.",al={"did lordaeron citizens survive","did anyone survive lordaeron fall","survivors of lordaeron"},it="people",add="2fe0baef"},{q="Why is there a city of undead under the ruins?",a="When the Lich King's power waned, Sylvanas Windrunner broke his mental control over a multitude of undead. Calling themselves the Forsaken, they overthrew the demonic dreadlords who held Capital City. The ruins above were too exposed to hostile eyes and constant attacks by the Scarlet Crusade, so Sylvanas chose to turn the vast subterranean crypts and sewers into a heavily fortified stronghold.",al={"why undercity exists","why is undercity under lordaeron","undead city under ruins"},it="place",add="9cf7434f",nx={14,15}},{q="Who built the Undercity?",a="The foundation began beneath Capital City as royal dungeons, sewers, and deep crypts constructed by the humans of Lordaeron. During the Third War, Arthas and the Scourge began expanding these underground corridors into an elaborate network intended to be a center of Scourge power. After wresting control from the dreadlord Varimathras, Sylvanas and the Forsaken finished carving out the Undercity as their permanent capital.",al={"who made undercity","undercity construction","who excavated undercity"},it="origin",add="55ddf3da"},{q="Was the Undercity always down there?",a="Not in its modern, sprawling state. In the days of King Terenas, the underground consisted merely of castle dungeons, aqueducts, sewer channels, and family tombs. Only after the kingdom fell did Scourge abominations and Forsaken laborers hollow out the massive rings and quarters you see today, turning utility tunnels into a sprawling underground bastion of the dead.",al={"was undercity always there","did undercity exist before","old undercity"},it="history",add="c0ee4f6f"},{q="Who's in charge here?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen, commands these ruins and the Undercity beneath them. Once the Ranger-General of Silvermoon, she was slain by Arthas, raised as a vengeful banshee, and eventually reclaimed her physical corpse. Through sheer willpower and cunning, she liberated her undead brethren and forged the Forsaken, guiding them with ruthless determination from her throne in the Royal Quarter.",al={"who rules lordaeron ruins","leader of undercity","who controls this place"},it="in_charge",add="dc41e367",nx={17,18}},{q="Is Sylvanas a queen or something else?",a="Her people revere her as the Banshee Queen and Lady of the Forsaken, but she is not hereditary royalty of Lordaeron. The title reflects the tragic nature of her death at the hands of Prince Arthas, who ripped her soul from her body to serve as a wailing banshee. Though the title echoes monarchy, her authority is born of liberation, survival, and total military command.",al={"is sylvanas a queen","banshee queen title","what is sylvanas title"},it="identity",add="3d3094f9"},{q="Does Sylvanas answer to Thrall?",a="On paper, Sylvanas recognizes Warchief Thrall as the supreme commander of the Horde, and she agreed to their alliance of convenience. In reality, the Banshee Queen maintains total autonomy over the Forsaken and their northern territories. Thrall's word is respected, and Forsaken emissaries walk Orgrimmar, but Lady Sylvanas answers first and foremost to her own survival and the ambitions of her people.",al={"sylvanas thrall relationship","does sylvanas obey thrall","is sylvanas under thrall"},it="leader",add="ac534dbb"},{q="What happened in that throne room up the stairs?",a="The throne room was the site of the catastrophic betrayal that ended the kingdom. Prince Arthas, freshly returned from Northrend, marched past welcoming citizens and ringing bells into this chamber. As his father, King Terenas, rose from the throne to greet him, Arthas drew Frostmourne, proclaimed that he was succeeding his father, and drove the cursed runeblade through the old king's heart.",al={"what happened in the throne room","lordaeron throne room story","throne room history"},it="history",add="6b51523d",nx={20,21}},{q="Is that the spot where Terenas was killed?",a="Yes. If you stand right before the broken dais, you are on the very flagstones where King Terenas Menethil II drew his last breath. A faint, dark stain remains visible on the stone floor, said to be the old king's blood that seeped into the masonry when his son struck him down. Even now, spectral whispers and bells echo faintly in the chamber.",al={"where was terenas killed","is that terenas blood","spot where king terenas died"},it="place",add="6e83c082"},{q="What happened to Terenas's crown?",a="Terenas's golden crown fell to the floor when Arthas murdered him in the throne room. Its fall marks the end of his reign and the catastrophe that overtook Lordaeron.",al={"why is the crown on the floor","king terenas crown ruins","terenas crown blood"},it="item",add="ea8d978d"},{q="Are the Forsaken actually part of the Horde?",a="Yes, though it is largely a pact of mutual survival. Surrounded by the Scarlet Crusade, hostile humans, and the remaining Scourge, the Forsaken sent ambassadors across the sea seeking allies. The Horde, needing a foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms to counter the Alliance, agreed to grant them entry, giving the Forsaken much-needed military backing and international standing.",al={"forsaken horde alliance","are undead in the horde","why are forsaken horde"},it="side",add="bb044bc8",nx={23,24}},{q="Why did Thrall accept undead into the Horde?",a="Thrall was swayed primarily through the intercession of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and the tauren, who believed the Forsaken were tragic victims who might one day find redemption or a cure for their affliction. Furthermore, Thrall recognized the strategic necessity of an established stronghold in the Eastern Kingdoms to prevent the Alliance from dominating the northern continent unchallenged.",al={"why did thrall allow undead","thrall forsaken reason","why horde took forsaken"},it="motive",add="50000697"},{q="Do the orcs and tauren trust them?",a="Not entirely. While the tauren view them with deep pity and hope to heal their condition, many orcs harbor deep misgivings about dark magic, necromancy, and the sinister nature of the Undercity. Thrall keeps a close watch on Sylvanas's actions, and stationed ambassadors are wary of what brews within the Royal Apothecary Society's laboratories.",al={"do orcs trust forsaken","tauren forsaken trust","does horde trust undead"},it="ties",add="9af0f393"},{q="Is it safe for me to be standing here?",a="It depends entirely on your loyalties. If you fight for the Horde, the Forsaken and their abominations recognize you as an ally, though the shadows above hold rogue creatures and lingering spirits. If you march beneath the banner of the Alliance, you are deep in enemy territory; Forsaken sentries and dread guards will strike you down on sight.",al={"is ruins of lordaeron safe","am i safe here","danger standing in lordaeron"},it="threat",add="849f698a",nx={26,27}},{q="Will the guards attack me?",a="Forsaken Deathguards and royal abominations stationed around the ruins will ignore or protect Horde travelers, but they are brutally hostile to Alliance champions. Additionally, hostile renegades and monsters lurk within isolated corridors and dungeon wings of the ruins above, and they will attack anyone who crosses their path regardless of allegiance.",al={"will undercity guards attack","are ruins guards hostile","do guards attack me"},it="hostile",add="aac358a1"},{q="Are there still Scourge nearby?",a="Yes. While Sylvanas swept the majority of the Scourge out of Capital City, the Scourge remains heavily entrenched just beyond the borders in the Western Plaguelands. Even within the darker alcoves and forgotten sub-levels of these ruins, mindless undead and Scourge remnants still linger, waiting to tear into any living flesh that wanders too far.",al={"scourge in lordaeron ruins","is the scourge near undercity","are there scourge nearby"},it="threat",add="e9ec8c01"},{q="What's the plague everyone keeps talking about?",a="They speak of the Plague of Undeath, a horrific bio-magical contagion developed by the Lich King and his necromancers. Distributed across Lordaeron through infected grain by the Cult of the Damned, it killed anyone who consumed it within hours and immediately reanimated their corpses as obedient, rotting thralls of the Scourge.",al={"what is the plague of undeath","what plague is mentioned","lordaeron plague"},it="threat",add="0a975308",nx={29,30}},{q="Who made the original plague?",a="The original plague was engineered by the dreadlords of the Burning Legion and perfected by the Lich King, Ner'zhul, while he was imprisoned atop the Frozen Throne in Northrend. To unleash it on Lordaeron, he enlisted the renegade Dalaran archmage Kel'Thuzad, who founded the Cult of the Damned and tainted the grain supplies.",al={"who created the plague of undeath","creator of original plague","who made plague"},it="origin",add="290f94a8"},{q="Is Sylvanas making a new one?",a="Yes. Lady Sylvanas has tasked the Royal Apothecary Society with brewing a 'New Plague.' Her goal is to craft a biological weapon potent enough to annihilate both the Scourge and the living alike, ensuring the survival of the Forsaken and vengeance against Arthas. Their secretive tests are taking place right now in the Apothecarium below.",al={"is sylvanas creating a plague","forsaken new plague","new plague undercity"},sp=1,it="purpose",add="89f62638"},{q="Who is the Lich King and what does he want?",a="The Lich King is the supreme ruler of the Scourge, created from the tortured spirit of the orc shaman Ner'zhul encased in ice atop the Frozen Throne. His goal was to soften Azeroth for the Burning Legion, but he harbored his own terrifying ambitions: to eradicate all mortal life and replace it with an eternal, unified empire of undeath under his absolute mental command.",al={"who is the lich king","what does lich king want","lich king motives"},it="threat",add="dcb566d2",nx={32,33}},{q="Where is the Lich King now?",a="He rules from the Frozen Throne atop Icecrown Glacier on the distant, frozen continent of Northrend. Following Illidan's assault that cracked his icy prison, the Lich King summoned Arthas back to Northrend to merge their spirits and preserve his power, far away from the shattered kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"where is lich king","lich king location","where is the frozen throne"},it="target",add="3a9893a7"},{q="Does he still control the Forsaken?",a="No. When the Frozen Throne was cracked by Illidan's spellwork, the Lich King's telepathic grip began to fracture. Sylvanas and many other undead regained their free will and broke away from his collective mind. Though he seeks to reclaim them, the Forsaken now violently resist his whispers and fight fiercely to maintain their autonomy.",al={"does lich king control forsaken","can lich king command forsaken","forsaken free will"},it="power",add="0138c577"},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade and why do they hate the undead?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is an order of religious, human zealots formed from the shattered remnants of the Silver Hand and Lordaeron's knights. Traumatized by the plague that destroyed their homeland, they are consumed by paranoia. In their eyes, all undead are abominations without exception, and anyone living who associates with them is considered tainted and marked for execution.",al={"who are scarlet crusade","why scarlet crusade hate undead","scarlet crusade lore"},it="threat",add="6a523c60",nx={35,36}},{q="Are they the same as the Argent Dawn?",a="No, they are bitter rivals with common roots. Both arose from the ashes of the Knights of the Silver Hand, but when the Scarlet Crusade succumbed to blind fanaticism and xenophobia, moderate paladins broke away to form the Argent Dawn. The Dawn welcomes all races and focuses on defending the land against the Scourge rather than purging indiscriminately.",al={"scarlet crusade vs argent dawn","are scarlet and argent dawn same","difference between scarlet and argent"},it="allies",add="b59db3a3"},{q="Do they attack living players too?",a="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade believes that anyone not clad in their crimson tabard is secretly harboring the plague or collaborating with the undead. Whether you are an orc, a tauren, a night elf, or a human soldier from Stormwind, their zealots will brand you a carrier of corruption and attack you on sight.",al={"does scarlet crusade attack alliance","do scarlets attack living","scarlet crusade hostile to living"},it="hostile",add="ca88b6f6"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society doing down there?",a="Operating out of the Apothecarium in the Undercity, this sinister guild of Forsaken alchemists and former mages works tirelessly under Lady Sylvanas's decree. Their primary mandate is developing a catastrophic 'New Plague' that can wipe out both the Scourge and the living races, conducting ruthless experiments to secure the Forsaken's supremacy.",al={"what does royal apothecary society do","royal apothecary society purpose","apothecaries undercity"},sp=1,it="purpose",add="861c7602",nx={38}},{q="Are they experimenting on people?",a="Yes. Deep within the Apothecarium, captured Scarlet Crusade crusaders, Scourge ghouls, and various beasts are locked away in iron cages. The apothecaries subject these prisoners to painful chemical cocktails and virulent plague strains, evaluating how quickly flesh rots and how the contagion affects both living and necrotic physiology.",al={"apothecary experimenting on humans","royal apothecary society experiments","are undercity apothecaries torturing people"},sp=1,it="threat",add="3c47ce18"},{q="Is Arthas still alive, and could I ever fight him?",a="Arthas is not dead in the mortal sense, but fully corrupted into a death knight champion of the Scourge. He is far across the sea in Northrend, beyond the reach of anyone in Lordaeron. Your fight right now is against the threats lingering here: the local Scourge commanders, the Scarlet Crusade, and the rogue beasts infesting these ruins.",al={"can i fight arthas","is arthas alive","will we face arthas"},it="next_step",add="f7d23701",nx={40}},{q="Is he the Lich King now?",a="Whispers from the north claim that Arthas ascended the spire of Icecrown to deliver the Lich King from Illidan's siege, shattering the ice to take up the Helm of Domination and merging his soul with Ner'zhul. To the world at large, the exact state of Northrend remains shrouded in icy mystery, but his dark presence hangs over all undead.",al={"is arthas the lich king","did arthas become lich king","arthas lich king identity"},sp=1,it="identity",add="9fc2648e"},{q="How did I end up in Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="You walked through the crumbling outer gates of the fallen capital in Tirisfal Glades, just above the elevators that descend into the Undercity. Whether you answered a military summons, pursued rumors of unchecked horrors clinging to the kingdom's corpse, or slipped past hostile territory to reclaim sacred remnants of the past, your journey brought you into the sealed, contested courtyards where the shadows of the Scourge and the ghosts of old humanity still linger.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","why am i in the ruins of lordaeron","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add="89a21402"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Ruins of Lordaeron?",a="You are here to purge the horrors festering in the surface ruins above the Forsaken capital. For the Horde, that means scouring rogue Scourge beasts, reclaiming lost insignias, and testing lethal concoctions for the Royal Apothecary Society. For the Alliance, it is an undercover strike to cleanse ancestral grounds, retrieve holy heirlooms like the Crest of Lordaeron, and bring solace to wandering, tormented ghosts who have not found peace.",al={"what am i doing here","what is my mission here","what should i do in the ruins","what's my goal here"},it="purpose",add="bb4abd7f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the ruins above are their former home and eternal graveyard. Clearing them secures their front door and supplies the apothecaries with components for developing the New Plague.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may see the ruined capital as hallowed ground stolen through betrayal, and seek lost heirlooms and a way to honor fallen kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can strike at the threshold of the Forsaken capital while bringing justice and peace to the spirits of your slaughtered northern brothers.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you walk the desecrated halls of Lordaeron, cradle of the Knights of the Silver Hand, to purge horrors and lay restless captains to rest in service to the Light."},kw={"bjork","lordaeron captain","new plague","rath'mael","ruins of lordaeron","the abandoned","the baron","tirisfal glades","undercity","viktor the vile","witherfang"},rel={"zone:undercity","topic:lordaeron","topic:light"},m={levels="15-20"},src={"Ruins of Lordaeron (instance)"}}
